+
+## 23. Chrome layout defects, reported from screenshots
+
+Four defects the owner photographed. All reproduced in the CSS.
+
+### F-50 · The header nav overprinted the brand and the icon buttons · **P0**
+
+Visible in the screenshot: "Gallery" and "Services" painted on top of
+"Ecowoods / TORONTO · EST. 2000", and the search and theme buttons painted on
+top of "Reviews" and "FAQ".
+
+`.brand-lockup` and `.topbar-cta` are both `flex: 0 0 auto` — they refuse to
+shrink. `.topbar-nav` was `flex: 1 1 auto; min-width: 0`, so it absorbed the
+entire shortfall and could shrink **below its own content width**. Its links are
+`white-space: nowrap`, so they did not wrap. And because the nav is
+`justify-content: center`, the overflow spilled out of **both sides at once** —
+left onto the brand, right under the buttons.
+
+That also explains the owner's note that "EST 2000 does not align". It aligns
+fine; it was being overprinted.
+
+Fixed structurally rather than by tuning a number:
+
+```css
+flex: 0 1 auto;
+min-width: max-content;   /* can no longer shrink below its own content */
+overflow: clip;           /* nothing can ever paint outside the nav's box */
+```
+
+### F-51 · The hamburger handover happened after the collision, not before
+
+`.topbar-nav { display: none }` fired at `max-width: 1023px`. With F-50's fix
+the nav can no longer hide a shortfall by shrinking, so the band from 1024px to
+roughly 1199px — eight nav labels plus the brand plus the CTA cluster — is
+exactly where it runs out of room.
+
+Raised to **1199px**. The hamburger sheet carries the same eight links, so
+nothing becomes unreachable; the header simply hands over while it still fits.
+
+### F-52 · The chat dock covered the footer's legal links · P1
+
+`ChatWidget.tsx:132` renders `.rg-dock` at `position: fixed`, `z-index: 130`,
+`bottom/right: var(--fab-inset)`. Scrolled to the bottom of the page it sits on
+top of `.footer-bottom` and covered **"Terms"** — one of two policy links, and
+the last thing a visitor reaches.
+
+`.footer-bottom` now reserves the dock's footprint
+(`64px + --fab-inset-x + 1rem`), **desktop only**. On mobile `--fab-inset` rises
+to 88px to clear the sticky CTA bar, so the dock already sits above this row and
+a ~96px gutter on a 320px screen would be worse than the defect.
+
+Moving the dock was rejected: it would fight the sticky CTA on mobile, which is
+a revenue control.
+
+### F-53 · The footer card's rounded corners read as a seam · P2
+
+`.site-footer` is an inset card with `border-radius: 28px 28px 0 0`. With no
+space above it, the curve cut directly against whichever section ended above —
+so it read as two edges meeting rather than as the page ending, which is the
+whole point of the pattern.
+
+Added `margin-top: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.5rem)` (and a matching mobile value) so
+the page background completes the corner.
